I'll start with the good because plenty of people are already bashing it. The gameplay mechanics are on point. The ways assists work requires learning, but once you get it down the way the game plays is refreshing to previous fighters including previous MvC titles. Much more has been done for game balance over all. Comboing is still involved and interesting without needing micro-procession timing to execute the more advanced combos. The stones add a unique mechanic both as the surge and storm. At first it may seem daunting and "game breaking" what the storms do, but give it time, experiement with each stone, both capabilities and you will see they are balanced against one another as well. I've been picking up fighters all through 2017 wishing something was at least decent and it wasn't until I picked this up (with very little expectations I may add) that I finally felt I found an actual quality fighting title.
Addressing the elephant in the room;
This game isn't nearly as bad as other want it to sound. The vissuals aren't the greatest, but they aren't nearly as bad as they are being made out to be. The DLC debate is an individual preference, the game is however complete without the additional characters as it has all modes and game functions as inteded whether you pick up the extra characters or not.
